    {
        "content": "<p>xia-chao removed the review request for <a href=\"https://github.com/orgs/bytecodealliance/teams/wasmtime-default-reviewers\">wasmtime-default-reviewers</a> from <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14908\">PR #14908</a>.</p>",
        "id": 633705370,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792600359
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>alexcrichton <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14908#issuecomment-6321037815\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14908\">PR #14908</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>For something that's roughly intended to be a debugging-ish server this feels like <code>wasmtime serve</code> is starting to sprawl quite a lot -- for example custom I/O implementations, hardcoded HTTP prefixes and such, this all feels pretty intense for what is otherwise intended to be a relatively simple wrapper around <code>hyper</code> and <code>wasmtime</code> together. Is it possible to simplify this and/or externalize the complexity? For example I see that <code>hyper-util</code> has utilities for handling either 1.1 or 2 connections, that might be appropriate?</p>\n<p>Also, is this valid? I thought that http/2 required TLS and AFAIK we don't have any configuration to have <code>wasmtime serve</code> serve over TLS.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 633706365,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792600569
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>xia-chao <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14908#issuecomment-6321197370\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14908\">PR #14908</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>i'm pretty sure h2c is valid ,rfc 9113 has prior knowledge for cleartext, http/2 doesn't need tls. ran curl --http2-prior-knowledge and got a 200.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 633706796,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792600668
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>xia-chao <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14908#issuecomment-6321454005\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14908\">PR #14908</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<blockquote>\n<p>For example I see that <code>hyper-util</code> has utilities for handling either 1.1 or 2 connections, that might be appropriate?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>i first tried hyper util, then went dep free (the branch name says nodep). using hyper util would probably be less code to maintain long term ok to add it?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 633709758,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792601274
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>fitzgen removed the review request for <a href=\"https://github.com/fitzgen\">fitzgen</a> from <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14908\">PR #14908</a>.</p>",
        "id": 634078225,
